{"agent":"lane-sched-order","data":{"alternatives":"","consequences":"","context":"D-priority-semantics cited a knob [schedule].order that did not exist (bug B0db4e156e8); SCHED-order-knob adds it.","decided_by":"lane-sched-order","decision":"A task or phase PRIORITY is a number where LOWER runs sooner (1 before 100). The scheduler offers ready work by the keys of [schedule].order, left to right; the shipped default is today's order: recover_first, bugs_first, unphased_first, priority ascending, id (core/schedule/_filters.py ORDER). Also selectable, not in the default: critical_path, waited, phase_priority, wave. id is always last as the deterministic tie-break; an unknown or repeated key is refused naming the known ones. [schedule].order_pin pins keys to the head and is tighten-only across layers (a company floor can keep bugs_first first). bugs_first = false is the bool shortcut that makes the bugs_first key neutral. Everything else of D-priority-semantics stands: a fix-<bug> item outranks any feature, a priority change is a queue edit that needs a reason, ties are broken by id.","dedupe":{"answer":"new","candidates":[{"id":"D-priority-semantics","score":0.603574251},{"id":"SCHED-order-knob","score":0.542021143},{"id":"B0db4e156e8","score":0.45656943}],"score":0.603574251},"globs":["ddflow/core/schedule/_filters.py","ddflow/config_sections/schedule.py"],"item":"SCHED-order-knob","saw":["D-rule-dedupe-everywhere","D-trigger-cap-knob","D-agent-caps","D-rename-keeps-alias","D-everything-configurable","D-small-files","D-universal-principles","D-shared-engines-r2","D-ai-import","D-constellation","D-platform-mcp","D-stack-tools","D-acp-r2","D-model-routing","D-company-workflows","D-file-ddflow-defects","D-ddflow-self-assessment-r2","D-config-engine","D-merge-order-warn-r2","D-unify-r2","D-config-layer-order","D-jinja-trust-reaffirmed","D-written-defaults-are-marked","D-load-and-parallel-defaults","D-no-deletion","D-US-answers","D-optimizer-answers","D-no-shell-principle","D-small-files-30k","D-extension-contract-answers","D-rules-expansion-2026-11","D-external-frontends","D-scale-answers","D-fast-track-answers","D-reimpl-answers","Dc8cd2b6d22","D4596ece18d"],"sources":[],"status":"accepted","supersedes":["D-priority-semantics"],"tags":[],"title":"Priority and ordering: lower number runs sooner; the order keys are the [schedule].order knob"},"id":"e86ecf77decc9053903753e87","kind":"decision.recorded","lamport":192787,"schema":1,"subject":"D-priority-semantics-2","ts":"2026-11-13T10:35:39.170878Z"}
